  (text "Power subsystem -- USB-C 5V in, single 3.3V rail (pilink-7el.2)\nRP2350B's internal switched regulator makes its own 1.1V core voltage\nfrom this 3.3V rail (same pattern as stock Pico boards) -- no separate\n1.1V regulator on this sheet. +5V arrives from the USB-C sheet\n(pilink-7el.7); PWR_FLAG marks it as externally driven for ERC." (at 60.96 30.48 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 05f9001f-68b4-41c9-b633-340747c14553)
  )

  (text "U1: AMS1117-3.3, SOT-223, 1A LDO. JLCPCB Basic part C6186 / LCSC C6186,\nstock in the hundreds of thousands of units (checked 2026-11-14).\nFunctionally/pin equivalent to the NCP1117-3.3 used in Raspberry Pi's own\nofficial RP2350B minimal reference design (arturo182/rp2350_minimal_kicad\nmirror of RP-006442-DD-2, RP2350_80QFN_minimal.kicad_sch)." (at 60.96 46.99 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 7e9033c0-519c-4359-a2c3-9f2f753fbe3f)
  )

  (text "Decoupling: C1/C2 10uF bulk on regulator input/output, matching both the\nAMS1117 datasheet's minimum output-cap requirement and the 10uF bulk caps\n(C1/C5) on the same reference design's VBUS/VDD3V3 rail. C3 100nF local\nceramic at the 3V3 point-of-load, per Raspberry Pi's RP2350 Hardware\nDesign Guide (RP-008280-DS, Sec. 2.2.1): 100nF close to VDD pins, plus\nbulk capacitance per power domain." (at 60.96 160.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 54487828-8fea-454b-a628-566a5c551201)
  )

  (text "Out of scope for this sheet (lives on the RP2350B + Memory sheet,\npilink-7el.3): the ~11 individual 100nF decouplers on each of RP2350B's\nVDD3V3/IOVDD pins, and the VREG_LX/VREG_AVDD inductor+caps for the\nchip's internal 3.3V->1.1V switched-mode core regulator -- same split\nas Raspberry Pi's own reference design, just on a different sheet." (at 60.96 177.8 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 4f509b76-bf21-47f2-b154-7483f0eb276e)
  )
)
